---
import { DESKTOP, MIRROR, MIRRORED } from '../lib/discord';

const ASSETS = 'https://assets.sunbird.tools/plugins';
---

<section class="group">
   <div class="group-head">
      <h2>Desktop</h2>
   </div>
   <div class="box desktop">
      <p class="note">
         <b>Install Discord Phoenix first.</b>{' '}Sunbird starts it with the runtime loaded and
         updates itself on every launch. Discord's own files are never changed, so Discord updates
         don't undo it.
      </p>
      <p class="warn" role="note">
         <b>The plugin runtime is experimental.</b>{' '}It hooks into Discord's internals, so a
         Discord build it hasn't seen yet can crash on startup or break features. If Discord crashes
         or misbehaves with Sunbird, use access gate only below.
      </p>

      <div class="os">
         <h3>Discord Phoenix</h3>
         <p class="note">
            Build 2233 from {new URL(MIRROR).host}, a third-party mirror Sunbird does not run.
            Compare the SHA-256 of what you download with the one listed here.
         </p>
         <ul class="builds">
            {DESKTOP.map((build) => (
                  <li>
                     <a class="button dl" href={`${MIRROR}/${build.path}`}>
                        {build.name}
                     </a>
                     <code>{MIRRORED[build.path]}</code>
                  </li>
               ))}
         </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="os">
         <h3>Windows</h3>
         <a
            class="button dl"
            href={`${ASSETS}/sunbird-windows-x86_64.exe`}
            download="SunbirdSetup.exe"
         >
            Download for Windows
         </a>
         <p class="note">
            Run it once. It installs to <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Sunbird</code> and adds a Sunbird
            shortcut to the Start Menu and Desktop. Uninstall with{' '}
            <code>sunbird.exe --uninstall</code>{' '}in that folder.
         </p>
      </div>

      <div class="os">
         <h3>Linux</h3>
         <pre>curl -fsSL {ASSETS}/sunbird-linux.sh | sh</pre>
         <p class="note">
            It finds <code>discord-phoenix</code> on your <code>PATH</code> or a{' '}
            <code>discord-desktop*.AppImage</code>{' '}in <code>~/Applications</code> or{' '}
            <code>~/Downloads</code>. To use another AppImage, end the command with{' '}
            <code>sh -s -- /path/to/AppImage</code>. It adds a Sunbird entry to your app menu. To
            uninstall, end it with <code>sh -s -- --uninstall</code>.
         </p>
      </div>

      <div class="os">
         <h3>Access gate only</h3>
         <p class="note">
            Gets you past Discord's access gate without loading plugins or hooking anything else.
            It's the safe option when the plugin runtime crashes.
         </p>
         <p class="note">
            <b>Windows:</b>{' '}run <code>sunbird.exe --no-runtime</code>{' '}in{' '}
            <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Sunbird</code>. The shortcuts load the runtime, so add{' '}
            <code>--no-runtime</code>{' '}to a shortcut's target to keep using it.
         </p>
         <p class="note"><b>Linux:</b>{' '}install with</p>
         <pre>curl -fsSL {ASSETS}/sunbird-linux.sh | sh -s -- --no-runtime</pre>
         <p class="note">
            The Sunbird app menu entry then opens only the access gate. Run the plain install
            command again to get plugins back.
         </p>
      </div>
   </div>
</section>

<style>
.desktop {
   display: grid;
   gap: 16px;
   padding: 16px;
}

.os {
   display: grid;
   gap: 10px;
   padding-top: 16px;
   border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.warn {
   margin: 0;
   padding: 10px 12px;
   font-size: 13.5px;
   color: var(--warn);
   background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 8%, var(--surface));
   border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 35%, var(--border));
   border-radius: var(--radius);

   & b {
      font-weight: 600;
   }
}

h3 {
   margin: 0;
   font-size: 14px;
   font-weight: 650;
}

.dl {
   width: 100%;
}

.builds {
   display: grid;
   gap: 10px;
   margin: 0;
   padding: 0;
   list-style: none;

   & li {
      display: grid;
      gap: 6px;
   }

   & code {
      font: 11.5px / 1.4 var(--mono-family);
      color: var(--muted);
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
   }
}

pre {
   margin: 0;
   padding: 10px 12px;
   overflow-x: auto;
   font: var(--mono);
   color: var(--text);
   background: var(--bg);
   border: 1px solid var(--border);
   border-radius: var(--radius);
   user-select: all;
}
</style>
